language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_039_rehearsal: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A concert consists of a number of pieces of music of different durations, each involving a different combination of the members of the orchestra. Players arrive at rehearsals immediately before the first piece in which they are involved and depart immediately after the last piece in which they are involved. Find an order in which the pieces can be rehearsed so as to minimise the total time that players are waiting to play, that is the total time when players are present but not currently playing.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_039_rehearsal.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_039_rehearsal.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_039_rehearsal_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_039_rehearsal.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_039_rehearsal_1.param -run-solver

$ num_pieces: number of pieces
given num_pieces : int(1..)
$ num_players: number of orchestra members
given num_players : int(1..)
$ duration[k]: duration of piece k (indices 1-based: the data's piece 0 is 1)
given duration : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_pieces)] of int
$ rehearsal[p,k]: player p plays in piece k (1 if so; indices 1-based)
given rehearsal : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_players), int(1..num_pieces)] of int(0..1)

$ rehearsal_order[s]: the piece rehearsed in slot s, numbered from 0 as in the problem (indices 1-based: slot 1 is the first slot)
find rehearsal_order : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_pieces)] of int(0..num_pieces-1)
$ plays[p,s]: player p plays in the piece rehearsed in slot s (auxiliary, a function of the order)
find plays : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_players), int(1..num_pieces)] of bool
$ present[p,s]: player p is at the rehearsal in slot s, that is between the first and the last slot in which the player plays (auxiliary)
find present : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_players), int(1..num_pieces)] of bool

branching on [rehearsal_order]
minimising (sum p : int(1..num_players) . sum s : int(1..num_pieces) . toInt(present[p,s] /\ !plays[p,s]) * duration[rehearsal_order[s] + 1])
such that
$ every piece is rehearsed in exactly one slot
allDiff(rehearsal_order),
$ a player plays in a slot exactly when that player is involved in the piece rehearsed in it
forAll p : int(1..num_players) . forAll s : int(1..num_pieces) . (plays[p,s] <-> (rehearsal[p, rehearsal_order[s] + 1] = 1)),
$ a player is present in a slot when there is a slot at or before it, and a slot at or after it, in which the player plays
forAll p : int(1..num_players) . forAll s : int(1..num_pieces) . (present[p,s] <-> ((exists t : int(1..num_pieces) . (t <= s /\ plays[p,t])) /\ (exists t : int(1..num_pieces) . (t >= s /\ plays[p,t]))))
